OL,3,GNEWSA#200m taxpayer-funded trains sit
OL,4,Abarely used for three years
OL,5,
OL,6,FA new fleet of publicly funded trains
OL,7,Fthat cost more than #200m still remain
OL,8,Fmostly unused more than three years
OL,9,Fafter the first one was delivered.
OL,11,FThey were initially promised to be
OL,12,Ffully up and running by 2022 but
OL,13,FTransport for Wales' (TfW) boss has
OL,14,Fsaid he expects the tram-trains will be
OL,15,Fin full service by the end of 2027
OL,17,FData obtained by the BBC reveals that
OL,18,Fless than half of the 36 fleet - what
OL,19,FTfW call the "final piece" in their
OL,20,F#2bn South Wales Metro project - have
OL,21,Fpassed rigorous statutory testing.
OL,23,APub: 04-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
